          %title
          %p
            Michael Green is professor for theoretical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            at Cambridge. Together with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
            he is one of the founding fathers of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/people/m.b.green/"} webpage
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Green_%28physicist%29"} Wikipedia entry
          %h2#quotes Quotes
          %p
            On the computation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomaly+cancellation"} anomaly cancellation
            now known as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            (also known as
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "http://theory.caltech.edu/people/jhs/strings/str133.html"} The First Superstring Revolution
          %blockquote
            %p#WeMustBeGettingPrettyClose
              MICHAEL GREEN: I do remember a particular moment, when
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
              and I were talking at the blackboard and working out these numbers which had to fit, and they just had to match exactly. I remember joking with John Schwarz at that moment, because there was thunder and lightning – there was a big mountain storm in Aspen at that moment – and I remember saying something like, you know, “We must be getting pretty close, because the gods are trying to prevent us completing this calculation.” And, indeed, they did match.
          %p
            (Taken from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://www.scribd.com/document/185276/NOVA-The-Elegant-Universe-Transcript"} NOVA - The Elegant Universe - Transcript
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            Early argument that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            = succeed "-expressions" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} density
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            are of the form of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+characters"} Chern characters
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+D-brane+charge"} K-theory classification of D-brane charge
          %ul
            %li#GreenHarveyMoore97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+A.+Harvey"} Jeffrey A. Harvey
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
              = succeed "," do
                %em I-Brane Inflow and Anomalous Couplings on D-Branes
              %strong 14
              (1997) 47-52 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9605033"}> arXiv:hep-th/9605033
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0264-9381/14/1/008"} doi:10.1088/0264-9381/14/1/008
          %p
            Popular exposition of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %ul
            %li#Green86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Superstrings
              %p
                Scientific American Vol. 255, No. 3 (September 1986), pp. 48-63 (
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/24976036"}> jstor:24976036
                )
          %p
            On the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
          %ul
            %li#GreenSchwarz81
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetrical Dual String Theory
            %li#GreenSchwarz82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetrical Dual String Theory. 2. Vertices and Trees
            %li#GreenSchwarz84
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Covariant description of superstrings
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/193596"} spire:193596
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(84)92021-5"} arXiv;10.1016/0370-2693(84)92021-5
            %li#GreenSchwarz84b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Properties of the Covariant Formulation of Superstring Theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/196623"} spire:196623
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(84)90030-0"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(84)90030-0
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomaly+cancellation"} anomaly cancellation
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Anomaly Cancellation in Supersymmetric
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 10
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=10
                  Gauge Theory and Superstring Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/15583"} spire:15583
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(84)91565-X"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(84)91565-X
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+superstring"} heterotic superstring
            to 6 dimensions (see also at
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%281%2C0%29+SCFT"} D=6 N=(1,0) SCFT
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pete+West"} Pete West
              = succeed "," do
                %em Anomaly-free chiral theories in six dimensions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(85)90222-6"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(85)90222-6
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-M5+brane+bound+states"} M2-M5 brane bound states
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"} Neil Lambert
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Papadopoulos"} George Papadopoulos
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Dyonic
                  = succeed "-branes" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  = succeed "-branes" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+1)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9605146"} arXiv:hep-th/9605146
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
